<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1 These consolidated unaudited results are recommended by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board at their meetings held on January 30 2023. The statutory auditors of the Company carried out Limited Review on these results. 2 The Company operates in a single segment which is Generation of power through renewable sources and related services. 3 The corresponding previous period witnessed resumption of REC trading after 18 months, resulting in significant increase of Rs 4427 lakhs in revenues. 4 The group could not proceed with Phase III power project and is confident of recovering substantial portion of capital advances given. Hence, no provision is required for the capital advance amounting to Rs. 6511 lakhs. For the delay in recovery provision of Rs. 2549 lakhs made till December 31 2022. The above has been highlighted as an Emphasis of matter in the Limited Review Report. 5 Based on stay granted by the Hon’ble Supreme Court of India on the order of CERC on reduction of floor price, and based on the legal opinion obtained, the Group is confident of realizing Rs.2071 lakhs of receivables. For the delay in recovery provision of Rs. 466 lakhs made.   The above has been highlighted as an Emphasis of matter in the Limited Review Report. 6.During the previous quarter, the company proposed to raise equity capital through rights issue. The company received in-principle approval from the stock exchanges BSE and NSE and SEBI subject to compliance requirements. The company is in the process of filing the Letter of Offer. 7.The Financial results includes total income of Rs. 20 lakhs, total loss after tax of Rs. 210 lakhs for the nine months ended December 31 2022  in respect of two subsidiaries, whose financial statements were prepared by the Management on the basis other than that of going concern.  8.During December 2022 our promoters, M/s. Janati Bio Power Private Limited JBPL  informed the Stock Exchanges that 1.5 crore Shares of Company were invoked by M/s. Axis Trustee Services limited out of 4crore Shares pledged. The revised holding of JBPL is 32.48%.   9 Exceptional Items  Rs In lakhs   Particulars Quarter ended Nine months ended Year ended     31 Dec 22 30 Sep 22 31 Dec 21 31 Dec 22 31 Dec 21 31 Mar 22    Unaudited Unaudited Unaudited Unaudited Unaudited Audited    a Profit/(Loss) on sale of assets (Net) 848 48 (1) 2216 258 300    b Impairment (loss)/ reversal on assets classified as held for sale  0 0 0 32 0 (32)    c Differential Tariff claim 0 0 0 0 2441 2441    d Gain/(Loss) on modification of Lease 287 0 0 287 123 123    e Interest income/(expense) (net)  324 (527) 0 (704) 0 0    f Provision for reinforcement of foundation 289 0 0 (152) 0 0    Total 1748 (479) (1) 1679 2822 2832    10 During March 2022, the company disinvested its entire stake in Statt Orient Energy Private Limited. The investment was adequately provided for during earlier years. The repatriation of the sale proceeds of Rs. 57 lakhs is pending, full provision made on a prudent basis. 11 The Code on Social Security 2020 has been enacted and draft rules released. The actual impact on account of this change will be evaluated and accounted for when notification becomes effective. 12 Regrouping made wherever necessary to conform to current period presentation.   13 Financial Results of the Company  Standalone Rs In lakhs   Particulars Quarter ended Nine months ended Year ended    31Dec22 30Sep22 31Dec21 31Dec22 31Dec21 31Mar22   Unaudited Unaudited Unaudited Unaudited Unaudited Audited    Profit / (Loss) Before Tax 1485 (667) (248) 32 (791) (2,173)    Profit / (Loss) After Tax 1485 (667) (248) 32 (791) (2,173)</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
